replace(s['earnings_pattern'],[
(r'Home Depot stock rises 3% as retailer maintains full.year forecast','earnings','result',"Home Depot offers the most useful fresh contrast with the technology weakness: the market can reward an unchanged outlook when investors had feared a worse outcome. That is an expectations result rather than evidence of a universal consumer boom. The operating task is to keep sales profitable through financing-sensitive project demand. A maintained forecast can be valuable when it improves confidence in cash earnings, but the share reaction should not be projected mechanically onto another retailer with different customers and inventory."),
(r'Applied Materials. forecast hit by China pause|CoreWeave shares drop as growing losses eclipse AI demand surge','earnings',None,"The negative comparisons involve distinct hurdles. An equipment supplier can face access and timing constraints, while a capacity owner can have demand that is expensive to serve. Both weaken the case for treating industry enthusiasm as a sufficient earnings thesis. The equity needs a bridge through permitted deliveries, spending and financing to the cash retained by owners. A cheaper price does not make that bridge sound automatically; it changes the valuation question that needs to be answered."),
(r'Palo Alto Networks reports earnings beat|Nubank posts 42% profit boost','earnings',None,"The reported positives in a service franchise and a lender show that a growth-market drawdown need not mean all operating evidence has deteriorated. Investors can become more selective about the capital required to earn the next unit of profit. Compare recurring demand and cash conversion before deciding that the market has rejected an entire technology or financial theme. The more useful pattern is a higher burden of proof for expensive future earnings, with an opportunity in businesses already delivering a satisfactory return."),
(r'Robinhood launches NFL and college football prediction markets','retail',None,"The new platform product is a commercial development, but its eventual contribution to earnings remains to be demonstrated. Engagement, legal access and monetisation all belong in the bridge from announcement to shareholder value. A launch can be real while the profit forecast is still uncertain. Treat customer interest in the activity separately from evidence of investor interest in the stock. The equity deserves a larger allocation only when the opportunity survives the costs and constraints needed to make it available."),
(r'How retail accounting could distort profitability|Walmart and Target.s front-loading','earnings',None,"The next retail reports need a replacement-cost and inventory assessment before their margins are extrapolated. A result that benefits from goods bought under earlier conditions may be economically different from the next shipment sold at the same price. Keep pending events pending. Prefer a result that explains how demand reaches recurring cash, and reduce positions where a reassuring headline leaves a more demanding financing or cost problem unresolved. The earnings premium should reward durability, not merely the ability to tell a convincing industry story.")])
s['earnings_pattern']['title']='A maintained outlook can beat a grand growth promise'
s['underowned']=[]
for title,rows in [
('Retail execution inside a technology-led risk debate',[
('Attention Gap',r'Home Depot stock rises 3% as retailer maintains full.year forecast','earnings',"A consumer business delivering a more reassuring operating answer can be overlooked when the market conversation is dominated by technology valuation. The attraction is a specific earnings outcome, not a claim that institutions have a measured underweight to the sector."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'Home Depot stock rises 3% as retailer maintains full.year forecast','earnings',"Home Depot provides a focused project-demand exposure. A broader consumer fund introduces different customers and cost structures. The risk is that financing or household caution prevents the maintained outlook from becoming a durable cash result."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'Retail sales rise 0.5%|Consumer Sentiment Signals Caution','us_data',"Watch whether repeat demand remains profitable after any spending brought forward ahead of tariffs. Add where inventory and cash conversion validate the sales story; do not use a single positive retailer to underwrite the whole household cycle.")]),
('Copper projects need returns, not a growth slogan',[
('Attention Gap',r'KGHM stawia na Retków','poland_pl',"A named mining investment offers a tangible company-level development. Copper's infrastructure uses can make the product attractive without proving that every new project will earn an adequate return. The analytical opportunity is to map cost and execution more carefully than a broad commodity narrative does."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'BHP and Rio Tinto lobby Donald Trump over US copper mine','australia',"KGHM and international producers carry different project, jurisdiction and financing exposures. Permitting and construction delays can determine the shareholder outcome even when eventual customer demand is plausible. Avoid treating the metal price as a substitute for project valuation."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'KGHM stawia na Retków|BHP CEO Sanguine on Latest Setback','poland_pl',"Increase exposure only as funding, cost control and delivery make the cash-return bridge more credible. A demand story without attractive project terms is insufficient. Protect the risk budget if delays require more capital without a commensurate improvement in the expected shareholder claim.")]),
('The nuclear contract map beneath the sector story',[
('Attention Gap',r'Google announces Tennessee as site for small modular nuclear reactor','retail',"The named site gives the demand discussion more specificity. It also makes it easier to ask which party owns each economic claim, rather than buying an indiscriminate collection of nuclear-related securities. This is a commercial mapping problem rather than proof of an institutional exposure gap."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'Google, Kairos Power plan advanced nuclear|Morgan Stanley says nuclear power','retail',"Separate fuel, generation, development and regulated utility exposure. A quoted analyst preference does not turn an indirect thematic fund into the holder of the announced contract. Prefer the security whose financing and customer arrangements can actually be evaluated."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'Google announces Tennessee as site for small modular nuclear reactor','retail',"Track credible funding and the allocation of licensing and construction risk. The project becomes more valuable to shareholders as those obligations become workable. A growing electricity need can remain true while the equity return weakens because development costs or timing deteriorate.")]),
('Currency hedging as an explicit part of equity selection',[
('Attention Gap',r'Global Investors Cut Back on Dollar Hedging, State Street Says','europe',"The reported change in hedging behaviour matters because an international equity allocation contains a currency decision whether or not the investor writes it down. A correct local earnings thesis can receive a very different translated return. Treat that exposure as part of the trade design."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'Nasdaq tumbles, European shares rise|European shares muted','europe',"A European fund and a US growth holding can express relative valuation while carrying different currency risk. Choose hedged or unhedged implementation according to the intended return mechanism, rather than allowing the latest performance ranking to make that decision indirectly."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'Global Investors Cut Back on Dollar Hedging, State Street Says','europe',"Reassess if the exchange rate begins to dominate the local operating thesis or if the cost of hedging changes the expected return. The opportunity is more deliberate risk ownership, not a prediction that the reported behaviour of other investors will continue indefinitely.")])]:
 s['underowned'].append({'title':title,'parts':[[label,q(rx,topic)+text] for label,rx,topic,text in rows]})
replace(s['crypto'],[
(r'Bitcoin Price, XRP, Ethereum Fall|Bitcoin, ethereum slip as crypto markets pull back','crypto',None,"The decline is now a test of financing and conviction rather than another celebration of access. An asset can retain a plausible long-term use case while the marginal buyer becomes less willing to carry volatility. That is particularly important for a treasury equity whose funding terms and trading hours differ from the token it holds. Use the direct asset when the thesis is token demand, and evaluate the corporate wrapper separately on dilution, expenses and the premium paid for its balance sheet. A larger gross holding is not by itself a larger economic claim for each existing owner."+obs('BTC-USD',(1,20),'Bitcoin')+obs('ETH-USD',(1,20),'Ether')+obs('SOL-USD',(1,20),'Solana')),
(r'Wyoming.s .Frontier. Stablecoin Debuts|Illinois governor signs new crypto oversight laws','crypto',None,"New distribution and legal frameworks can expand the set of investable or usable products without eliminating commercial uncertainty. A launch and a supervisory rule solve different problems, and neither guarantees an immediate profitable use case for every related token or listed platform. Keep the precise event in view. The market becomes more attractive when improved access is accompanied by resilient demand and funding that does not rely on an ever higher price. During a pullback, that is a more useful confirmation than another ambitious forecast made during the earlier advance."),
(r'Ethereum treasury firm SharpLink stock dips|BitMine files to expand|SEC Punts','crypto',None,"Limit leverage and require a separate case for the wrapper premium. If financing becomes less generous, the equity can underperform even while the underlying asset stabilises. Conversely, an orderly token recovery does not automatically restore the economics of a company that issued shares on unattractive terms. Reduce the least transparent funding structures first when liquidity weakens. Add only when the investor can identify the return being purchased: token exposure, a platform service or a well-priced corporate capital-allocation mechanism. Those are distinct decisions, and a familiar narrative should not collapse them into one.")])
s['crypto']['title']='The reversal exposes the extra wager inside the wrapper'
replace(s['flows'],[
(r'Fed.s Bowman doubles down on her dissent|Fed.s Goolsbee sees.*unease','us_macro',None,"The policy conversation contains disagreement, which matters when asset prices have already capitalised a comfortable easing path. Different reactions to inflation and activity imply a range of plausible financing outcomes rather than a single assured direction. A portfolio built around cheap capital should therefore have more room for error than one funded internally by customer cash. Keep event exposure liquid enough to adjust after the message rather than borrowing against the preferred interpretation beforehand. The key distinction is whether policy improves viable borrowing or is responding to a demand deterioration that also damages the earnings being discounted."),
(r'Nasdaq tumbles, European shares rise|Options Traders Brace for Big Tech Selloff','us_macro',None,"The equity retreat alongside the bond observations shows why a rate move is an incomplete protection for a demanding valuation. Investors can lower the discount rate and still demand a larger premium for execution or financing risk. The dollar changes the transmission to foreign borrowers and international returns, adding another reason to keep exposures separate. A European relative-value allocation, a Treasury position and a US growth equity do not offer interchangeable payoffs. The portfolio becomes more robust when those distinctions are explicit rather than hidden under a single label of global liquidity."+obs('DX-Y.NYB',(20,),'DXY')+obs('TLT',(20,),'TLT')),
(r'CoreWeave.*(?:loss|financing)|Galaxy closes.*debt facility','flows',None,"Infrastructure financing remains a concrete test of who receives the return from the buildout. Access to debt can allow construction to proceed, while the equity still faces heavy investment and a delayed cash payoff. Prefer a capital structure whose economics remain viable under less generous assumptions about utilisation and future funding. Broad credit prices provide context but cannot certify an individual issuer. If credit stays orderly while a capital-intensive equity falls, the market may be reassessing the distribution of value rather than declaring that all financing has closed. That distinction should guide which exposure is reduced first."+obs('HYG',(20,),'HYG')+obs('LQD',(20,),'LQD')),
(r'Options Traders Brace for Big Tech Selloff With.*Disaster','flows',None,"The reported appetite for protective options belongs to the hedging discussion, not to an invented estimate of cash leaving every equity fund. Protection can be added while a long position remains in place. Meanwhile, changes in currency hedging can alter the return on an international allocation without a new stock purchase. Read the instrument and the horizon before interpreting a flow headline. A durable broadening of ownership would be more persuasive if earnings support expands with it; a narrow rally built on one financing assumption remains vulnerable even when the index itself is liquid."),
(r'Global Investors Cut Back on Dollar Hedging|Wall Street sees stock market rotation','europe',None,"Keep the risk budget capable of holding different outcomes. Maintain franchises with a defensible cash return, hold enough liquidity to take advantage of a repricing and avoid concentrating several positions in the same policy sensitivity. If the decline stays confined to expectations-heavy growth while credit and operating results remain sound, improve entry prices selectively. If the problem spreads to funding and customers, reduce gross exposure rather than relabelling every loss as a rotation. Review the currency received by the foreign allocation, because a relative equity thesis can be overwhelmed by an unintended exchange-rate position.")])
s['flows']['title']='A lower discount rate is not a complete hedge for an expensive promise'
scenario_rows=[
('Powell: what the funding market accepts',[
(r'Powell.s Jackson Hole speech|keynote speech could be next catalyst','us_macro',None,"The speech is pending and investors have different versions of the easing path in mind. The useful test is the financing response, not whether one sentence sounds reassuring. Keep the long end, credit and growth equities separate when deciding what the message actually changes."),
(r'Fed.s Bowman doubles down|Fed.s Goolsbee sees.*unease','us_macro',None,"If communication supports easier financing without destabilising inflation expectations, add to profitable borrowers and duration with clear earnings support. If funding remains demanding, reduce the weakest balance sheets first. Do not assume that a potential policy cut restores a high equity valuation automatically."),
(r'Options Traders Brace for Big Tech Selloff','flows',None,"The risk is paying twice for the same relief through a rate position and several expensive growth holdings. Maintain protection sized to the exposure actually owned. An operating disappointment can remain damaging even if the policy message is helpful, while a sound cash generator may survive an initially cautious speech.")]),
('Retail: the next company must answer its own cost question',[
(r'Powell.s Jackson Hole speech, Walmart earnings','earnings',None,"Home Depot's known result is a comparison rather than an answer for the remaining retailers. Different baskets and customers create different tariff and inventory effects. Keep the next announcements as uncertain events, and resist converting a favourable sector read-through into a reported beat that has not occurred."),
(r'How retail accounting could distort profitability|Walmart and Target.s front-loading','earnings',None,"Add where actual sales and margins survive an assessment of replacement costs and cash conversion. If current profitability relies on goods bought under earlier conditions, value the next period more conservatively. The trade should own durable operating quality rather than only a potentially flattering accounting window."),
(r'Consumer Sentiment Signals Caution|Retail sales rise 0.5%','us_data',None,"A customer can spend ahead of tariffs and then wait. That creates a timing risk to an otherwise plausible consumer thesis. Reduce the event position if its valuation requires both strong current demand and no later payback, while retaining room to buy an operating result that answers those questions credibly.")]),
('Intel: shareholder confidence meets the equity-swap question',[
(r'Intel.s Government Equity Swap Raises Eyebrows At Bernstein, But Retail Remains Confident','retail',None,"The fresh disagreement is explicitly about how support reaches owners. Confidence in the strategic business is not the same as agreement about the terms of a financing arrangement. The analyst concern and the retail confidence should remain attributed views rather than a declaration of a settled outcome."),
(r'Intel gets.*SoftBank equity investment','japan',None,"Retain a measured long bias if new capital improves a viable operating plan on terms that leave an attractive claim for existing owners. Reduce the holding if dilution or obligations absorb too much of the upside. Evaluate a named investment separately from any other prospective government arrangement."),
(r'Intel shares jump as Softbank|Intel secures.*SoftBank','japan',None,"A favourable reaction can raise the valuation hurdle before manufacturing economics improve. Do not transform a tactical financing catalyst into a permanent recovery assumption without another operating confirmation. The exit is a weaker expected shareholder return, even if the company remains strategically important and continues to attract public attention.")]),
('Peace talks: risk premium before verified cash flows',[
(r'European defence rally falters on Ukraine ceasefire talks|Nasdaq tumbles, European shares rise','europe',None,"The market can reprice diplomatic possibilities before an agreement exists. That changes the risk premium on assets with very different commercial exposures. A defence supplier, an energy producer and a European consumer business do not receive the same earnings outcome from the same headline."),
(r'European defence stocks send false peace signal|European defence rally falters','europe',None,"If a verified improvement reduces uncertainty while contracted demand remains sound, favour the company whose valuation has overreacted. If the operating outlook genuinely changes, reduce the exposure whose cash flows were being bought. Own specific economics rather than a broad label of peace or conflict."),
(r'oil.*(?:Ukraine|Russia|peace)|crude.*(?:Ukraine|Russia|peace)','sectors',None,"A commodity premium can fall faster than a corporate investment programme adjusts. Avoid financing a long-lived equity position with a short-lived headline assumption. Keep enough liquidity to revise the trade when verified facts replace diplomatic possibilities, and do not describe a proposed process as an accomplished settlement.")])]
for b,(title,rows) in zip(s['anticipatory'],scenario_rows):b['title']=title;replace(b,rows)
# Financial catalysts with the actual event status made explicit.
s['catalysts']=[]
for tk,title,st,rx,thesis,risk,trade in [
('PLTR','valuation criticism changes the expectations test','Mixed',r'Short.seller Andrew Left says OpenAI.s.*Palantir stock',"The new comparison is a named short seller's valuation argument, while the company's growth case remains visible in separate coverage. Treat the criticism as a view to evaluate rather than proof that the operating franchise has weakened.","The sharp price move makes position size central. A cheaper quote can improve entry terms without settling the appropriate multiple or the earnings path needed to support it.","Keep exposure measured and add only when valuation and cash earnings justify the same case. Cut a position if defending the growth narrative replaces an honest reassessment of the return available at the prevailing price."),
('INTC','support needs an acceptable shareholder claim','Bullish',r'Intel.s Government Equity Swap Raises Eyebrows|Intel gets.*SoftBank equity investment',"A named investment and fresh disagreement over possible support terms create a financial catalyst. The relevant question is how much of the operating upside remains available to existing owners after the capital required for the turnaround.","A strong reaction can make a strategically important company a less forgiving security. Support, customer execution and valuation all need to fit the same expected return.","Retain a limited positive bias where the financing improves execution on workable terms. Reduce it if the shareholder arithmetic deteriorates, even when the industrial programme continues to receive attention."),
('HD','the maintained outlook earns a company-specific reward','Bullish',r'Home Depot stock rises 3% as retailer maintains full.year forecast',"The known report provides a concrete operating and market response inside a selective consumer environment. The case is the company's ability to sustain its forecast, not a claim that every household-facing business shares the same result.","Demand remains sensitive to projects, financing and customer confidence. The positive reaction raises the burden for subsequent delivery and should not substitute for monitoring margins and cash.","Prefer a selective long holding while repeat demand supports the outlook. Reassess if financing relief fails to reach profitable activity or if inventory begins to absorb the cash that the recovery thesis requires."),
('HOOD','football broadens the product and regulatory test','Mixed',r'Robinhood launches NFL and college football prediction markets',"The platform has announced a specific product expansion. That establishes a commercial event, while the contribution to profits and the behaviour of investors in HOOD remain separate questions.","Customer activity needs to survive distribution and legal constraints. A larger opportunity does not guarantee an attractive margin after compliance, acquisition and operating costs.","Keep a watch position until engagement becomes viable earnings. Reduce exposure if regulatory or cost burdens absorb the product benefit; increase only when profitable platform economics support the valuation rather than a borrowed enthusiasm for the activity itself."),
('AMAT','China access remains an earnings constraint','Bearish',r'Applied Materials. forecast hit by China pause',"The forecast problem is tied to customer timing and export-license uncertainty. It is a specific revenue-access issue inside a broader semiconductor opportunity, requiring a more exact answer than another general declaration of AI demand.","A lower share price may compensate for uncertainty only when the revenue range and capital needs can be assessed. Avoid treating a possible future permission as an already earned sale.","Avoid adding longs until access or alternative customer demand provides a firmer earnings bridge. Reconsider when the company can demonstrate a viable return through the constraint, rather than when the surrounding industry narrative becomes louder."),
('NVDA','the next result still has to be delivered','Mixed',r'Morgan Stanley maintains bullish stance on Nvidia|Nvidia.s AI Chip Demand Fuels Higher Earnings Projections',"The catalyst is an upcoming result against confident projections. The preview is evidence of expectations, not a realised beat. Customer demand, permitted deliveries and margins must still produce the operating answer investors want.","A high-quality franchise can offer an uncomfortable event payoff when the security assumes too much. Keep the valuation hurdle distinct from admiration for the product and its customer base.","Hold a position sized for an uncertain announcement. Increase only where the actual result and outlook justify the price; cut exposure if the return case needs a policy or delivery assumption that management cannot support.")]:
 s['catalysts'].append({'title':'$'+tk+' — '+title,'stance':st,'parts':[['Catalyst & Thesis',q(rx)+thesis],['Price Hurdle & Risk',obs(tk,(1,20),tk)+risk],['Trade Expression',trade]]})
(R/'specs'/f'{D}.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
